    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras are prioritizing high-upside speed and favorable matchups today, anchored by **Trea Turner** (67.66) and **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (67.31), our two highest-projected starters. **Trea Turner** gains significant value today due to a favorable matchup against Peralta\u2019s slow delivery, which creates an elite environment for his stolen base production\u2014a key focus given the scarcity of speed in this league. Meanwhile, **Pete Crow-Armstrong** is positioned for a breakout day against the struggling Corbin; despite the platoon disadvantage, the SP skill differential (+15%) makes him an essential start. We also see high floor contributions from **Kyle Schwarber** (63.04) and **Yordan Alvarez** (62.94), whose elite xwOBA metrics allow them to remain \"Strong\" plays despite facing left-handed starters.\n\nThe most difficult bench decision involved **Junior Caminero** (58.99), who narrowly missed a \"Strong\" designation. While **Junior Caminero** offers solid power, the combination of a park factor drag and a slightly tougher matchup against Cavalli forced the optimizer to favor the lineup versatility provided by **Kazuma Okamoto** (60.37). We are keeping a close eye on **Caleb Durbin** (49.56) today; while he is currently in the lineup, his status is \"Lineup Pending,\" and if he drops in the order or is moved to the bench, we risk losing his critical stolen base upside against Hancock. We remain cautious with **Carson Benge** (41.02), who faces a tough assignment against S\u00e1nchez; his score is suppressed by the platoon disadvantage, making him the most likely candidate for a late-game swap should we need to protect our game caps if the contest turns into a blowout.",
